<title>FRANCE: SOCCER-FRANCE AND ITALY DRAW 2-2 IN LAST TOURNOI MATCH.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-FRANCE AND ITALY DRAW 2-2 IN LAST TOURNOI MATCH.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>France and Italy drew 2-2</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0) in the closing match of the Tournoi de France on</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>France - Zinedine Zidane 12, Youri Djorkaeff 72</p>
<p>Italy - Pierluigi Casiraghi 61, Alessandro Del Piero 90</p>
<p>penalty</p>
<p>Attendance: 28,500</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>France - 1-Lionel Charbonnier; 15-Lilian Thuram, 4-Franck</p>
<p>Leboeuf, 8-Marcel Desailly (18-Bruno N'Gotty 84), 12-Bixente</p>
<p>Lizarazu; 13-Ibrahim Ba, 19-Christian Karembeu (17-Patrick</p>
<p>Vieira 66), 7-Didier Deschamps, 10-Zinedine Zidane; 22-Florian</p>
<p>Maurice (6-Youri Djorkaeff 63), 9-Christophe Dugarry.</p>
<p>Italy - 12-Gianluca Pagliuca; 23-Attilio Lombardo,</p>
<p>14-Alessandro Nesta, 6-Alessandro Costacurta (16-Stefano Torrisi</p>
<p>46), 5-Fabio Cannavaro, 3-Paolo Maldini; 7-Angelo Di Livio,</p>
<p>11-Gianfranco Zola (13-Christian Panucci 56), 8-Roberto Di</p>
<p>Matteo; 9-Pierluigi Casiraghi (19-Christian Vieri 77),</p>
<p>20-Alessandro Del Piero.</p>
<p>Referee: Antonio Lopez Nieto (Spain)</p>
<p>    Final standings:   P  W  D  L  F  A  Pts</p>
<p> England		   3  2  0  1  3  1  6</p>
<p> Brazil		    3  1  2  0  5  4  5</p>
<p> France		    3  0  2  1  3  4  2</p>
<p> Italy		     3  0  2  1  5  7  2</p>
